<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Breaking news from AFRICA, Maghreb and Sub-Saharan Africa - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24’s coverage of events, politics and social issues across Africa, including North Africa (the Maghreb) and the Sahel, aided by our network of correspondents and experts across the continent.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/africa/rss</id><updated>2026-08-30T15:57:07Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Niger junta puts down mutiny with help from Russia's Africa Corps</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:36f63138f07cdc286f0eaecf94736c2603103fcf6429712e7db19c2026376fb1</id><updated>2026-08-30T15:57:07Z</updated><published>2026-08-30T15:20:01Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20260830-niger-junta-aided-by-russian-paramilitary-forces-regains-control-after-mutiny" /><summary type="html">Life returned to normal in Niger's capital on Sunday, a day after mutineers stormed the presidential palace and a military base at Niamey's main airport, resisting forces loyal to the ruling junta until Russia’s Africa Corps intervened. State TV reported that dozens of soldiers were killed or arrested, with some paraded in front of cameras live on television.</summary><category term="Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Niger: Junta says back in control after mutiny</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:57e04a6195f082a72979f3e0a86aab6e1d56c3d6b2b4f75de80c28022dafdecc</id><updated>2026-08-30T15:57:07Z</updated><published>2026-08-30T08:41:57Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/niger-junta-says-back-in-control-after-mutiny--b01e157aa8c7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/niger-junta-says-back-in-control-after-mutiny" /><summary type="html">Gunfire and explosions have been reported in Niger, as mutinying soldiers attempted to storm the presidential palace in the capital, Niamey, in a challenge to the ruling junta. The government said it had regained control after hours of fighting on Saturday. Léo Paichard and Nick Rushworth report.</summary></entry><entry><title>Niger's junta says 'regaining control' after clashes in capital</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a24aaa8581487764b1c8f60bcce1cc27acbdb2c2bb5b9f5414fc9f9b6395af9f</id><updated>2026-08-30T15:57:07Z</updated><published>2026-08-29T12:33:03Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/niger-s-junta-says-regaining-control-after-clashes-in-capital--2bf7e08a1a7f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/niger-s-junta-says-regaining-control-after-clashes-in-capital" /><summary type="html">Niger's ​defense ​ministry said the armed forces were ​progressively ‌retaking ⁠control ‌of sites targeted in ⁠an overnight attack on ​the ‌capital Niamey, according to a ‌statement read ​on state television, which resumed broadcasting ​on ​Saturday after ​temporarily going ​offline.</summary></entry><entry><title>Niger junta regains control after mutiny with help from Russian paramilitary forces</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cbc46e26f4788839cd22743c9e7814bf8d57c637819981ccbb3bf417c6f0a87e</id><updated>2026-08-30T15:57:07Z</updated><published>2026-08-29T06:33:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/africa/20260829-gunfire-and-explosions-heard-near-military-base-in-niger-s-capital--2f45acce54fa.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20260829-gunfire-and-explosions-heard-near-military-base-in-niger-s-capital" /><summary type="html">Niger's junta said Saturday it was back in control after mutineers held soldiers hostage at a military base next to the capital's airport. Russian Africa Corps paramilitary forces helped members of Niger's presidential guard recapture the air base, killing some of the mutineers, according to diplomatic and security sources.</summary><category term="Africa" /></entry><entry><title>DRC President Tshisekedi calls for national dialogue excluding M23 rebels</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:364bb0fcfc1049ad3cd8ec5263c51bb39612b6eb70362a6ad8e6636c610e96cd</id><updated>2026-08-30T15:57:07Z</updated><published>2026-08-28T20:36:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/eye-on-africa/20260828-drc-president-tshisekedi-calls-for-national-dialogue-excluding-m23-rebels--ac8f13394274.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/eye-on-africa/20260828-drc-president-tshisekedi-calls-for-national-dialogue-excluding-m23-rebels" /><summary type="html">In the Democratic Republic of Congo, President Félix Tshisekedi calls for a national dialogue to ease tensions, while excluding M23 rebels from taking part, as the government plans to suspend 11 public universities in rebel-controlled areas. Meanwhile, in Ghana, 23 people, including 11 children, have died after falling into abandoned illegal gold-mining pits, as the country faces an unprecedented surge in galamsey operations. Finally, in Cameroon, US deportees face uncertainty and fears of persecution as they await decisions on their asylum claims, following controversial deals by Washington with at least 30 countries to accept people it cannot legally deport directly to their home countries.</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Uganda's King of Tooro, once world's youngest reigning monarch, dies at 34</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2efd1f07a8288929872591b66187fc9236c0c18ff607aef97a9aa7dcc8d975a3</id><updated>2026-08-30T15:57:07Z</updated><published>2026-08-28T09:52:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/africa/20260828-uganda-s-king-of-tooro-once-world-s-youngest-reigning-monarch-dies-at-34--48846a82350f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20260828-uganda-s-king-of-tooro-once-world-s-youngest-reigning-monarch-dies-at-34" /><summary type="html">King Oyo Nyimba, leader of the Tooro kingdom in western Uganda, has died at the age of 34, the region's prime minister of his kingdom announced Thursday. Crowned at three years old, he became the world's youngest reigning monarch in 1995.</summary><category term="Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Nigeria's lucrative business of kidnappings</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:72e793dcc57e73d6b0db118e2c7f3b50be0736b4a6e3c1b2643e7ef25a5ffd6c</id><updated>2026-08-30T15:57:07Z</updated><published>2026-08-27T20:49:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/nigeria-the-lucrative-business-of-kidnappings--b7681c405c06.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/nigeria-the-lucrative-business-of-kidnappings" /><summary type="html">In tonight's programme, we speak to a Lagos analyst behind a new report laying out the figures behind abductions. Also, Tanzania's ruling party kicks the vice-president out even after he announces his plans to step down next week. Finally, in Senegal, the first African-manufactured generic drug to treat sickle cell disease is raising hopes of better treatment and reduced reliance on costly imported medicine.</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Wildfires kill 12 in Algeria as severe heatwave sweeps North Africa</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0aefeb067e4600622ddf6c41e448b21cde83b7a4f210c10d3e3ecc189a2763bb</id><updated>2026-08-30T15:57:07Z</updated><published>2026-08-26T23:46:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/africa/20260826-wildfires-algeria-severe-heatwave-sweeps-north-africa--aed0a3051f42.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20260826-wildfires-algeria-severe-heatwave-sweeps-north-africa" /><summary type="html">Twelve people died and dozens were injured as wildfires tore through northern Algeria on Wednesday, with authorities battling more than 150 blazes amid a scorching heatwave sweeping across North Africa. Six of the 54 injured were in critical condition and receiving intensive care.</summary><category term="Africa" /></entry><entry><title>New revelations at South Africa corruption inquiry</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2730cf0044a74483cc0ccd134b667df7dcb331b0c0991f70cb2efb380dbf6f30</id><updated>2026-08-30T15:57:07Z</updated><published>2026-08-26T20:48:12Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/south-africa-kingpin-and-the-corruption-commission--d0c22de924b9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/south-africa-kingpin-and-the-corruption-commission" /><summary type="html">In tonight's programme: The three-day testimony of an alleged underworld kingpin exposes the deep links between alleged criminals and high-profile police officers in South Africa. Also, in Tunisia, grieving families bid farewell to the young victims of a boat that went down in the Mediterranean Sea over the weekend. Finally, in an era of mass production and electric machines, one young Kenyan fashion designer is taking a slower approach.</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Mawlid festivities cancelled in Tigray over drone attacks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:da101c9e82d3c30ceb09d4ae6c413812a7380ea447d1298a125f2a866c153990</id><updated>2026-08-30T15:57:07Z</updated><published>2026-08-25T20:45:05Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/mawlid-cancelled-in-tigray--668d53805925.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/mawlid-cancelled-in-tigray" /><summary type="html">In tonight's programme: Muslims celebrate Mawlid across Africa but festivities are cancelled in Tigray because of recent drone attacks. But first: the United States calls for beefed-up UN sanctions against the warring parties in Sudan. Finally, in the Kenyan village of Cheporor, a recent discovery of gold sends thousands of amateur prospectors rushing to the area.</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Nigeria’s president orders rescue operation after mass kidnapping at mosque</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:eb4df752f6f31cd6f8af7a5cce6900e17b32273d9426aab6d6456397926f34c4</id><updated>2026-08-30T15:57:07Z</updated><published>2026-08-25T17:10:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/africa/20260825-nigeria-president-orders-rescue-after-mass-kidnapping-during-mosque-attack--e37e32f460dc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20260825-nigeria-president-orders-rescue-after-mass-kidnapping-during-mosque-attack" /><summary type="html">Nigerian President Bola Tinubu on Tuesday ordered security agencies to conduct a rescue operation after the mass kidnapping of worshippers during an attack on a mosque in the north-central Niger State last week. Local authorities were still trying to verify the number of missing people, but local residents said roughly 600 women, children and elderly people had been abducted.</summary><category term="Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Meet the young Kenyan designer preserving culture through traditional craft</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:382a7d6a53508de64072a9289d543b8bc8ef3edffa9ed962c14c8375c6934e15</id><updated>2026-08-30T15:57:07Z</updated><published>2026-08-25T12:19:46Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260825-meet-the-young-kenyan-designer-preserving-culture-through-traditional-craft--56285aab4f82.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260825-meet-the-young-kenyan-designer-preserving-culture-through-traditional-craft" /><summary type="html">At a time when fashion is increasingly dominated by mass production, a young Kenyan designer is taking a slower approach. Hillary Mukabwa, the founder and lead designer of Mukabwa Studio in Nairobi, works with hand looms to create cotton fabrics that he turns into clothes, bags and more in a deliberate attempt to reconnect with a craft increasingly being pushed aside by modernisation.</summary></entry><entry><title>DR Congo sees breakthrough as officials and rebels agree to peace talk roadmap</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1fb3cf7bcb204f00d1ff5927897f269c6e249b1f460e32ccec11712d1adb1680</id><updated>2026-08-30T15:57:07Z</updated><published>2026-08-25T09:24:14Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/dr-congo-sees-breakthrough-as-officials-and-rebels-agree-to-peace-talk-roadmap--ad1353917ba7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/dr-congo-sees-breakthrough-as-officials-and-rebels-agree-to-peace-talk-roadmap" /><summary type="html">In eastern Democratic Republic of Congo, Rwanda-backed M23 rebels are still in control of swathes of territory. After months of stalled peace talks, both sides have agreed to get the ball rolling again. FRANCE 24's Emmet Livingstone, in Kinshasa, has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Zambia shuts down court system</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:914390538cff77789a343b09d9b85e780a6b7dd6dbea6fb4548c4ef6aa3a950b</id><updated>2026-08-30T15:57:07Z</updated><published>2026-08-24T20:58:42Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/zambia-shuts-down-court-system--978a535ed1c3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/zambia-shuts-down-court-system" /><summary type="html">In tonight's programme: Human rights groups and the law association demand an explanation as Zambia completely shuts down its court system. Also, in Guinea, rescuers are still trying to unearth victims of a deadly landfill collapse. Finally, Nigeria wishes Ogogo on his way. The veteran star of the Nollywood screen is buried before heartbroken crowds in his hometown after passing away from cancer at 66.</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Ceasefire verification mission deploys to eastern DR Congo</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ce3fbd2390704008d8df693247aaedd42a1b688b1a735f4a68f9c18a66dbca95</id><updated>2026-08-30T15:57:07Z</updated><published>2026-08-24T16:04:37Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/africa/20260824-ceasefire-verification-mission-deploys-eastern-dr-congo--bb5511ed17ba.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20260824-ceasefire-verification-mission-deploys-eastern-dr-congo" /><summary type="html">A ceasefire verification mission comprised of representatives from DR Congo's government, the Rwanda-backed AFC/M23 rebel group, and observers from the International Conference on the Great Lakes Region (ICGLR) member nations arrived in South Kivu on Monday. The deployment came a day after the DRC and AFC/M23 agreed on a Switzerland-mediated roadmap for peace talks.</summary><category term="Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Guinea searches for survivors after landfill landslides kill 30</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dc84ac3060d06ef4a19a543a6f0cb93b85a9abc210365bb82a7dde6572523977</id><updated>2026-08-30T15:57:07Z</updated><published>2026-08-24T12:42:59Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/guinea-searches-for-survivors-after-landfill-landslides-kill-30--8fc640a061df.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/guinea-searches-for-survivors-after-landfill-landslides-kill-30" /><summary type="html">In Guinea, a landslide at a garbage dump outside the capital Conakry has claimed the lives of at least 30 people. The government of the West African country says it has mobilised significant resources to try and find survivors that may still be trapped under massive piles of waste. Less than a week ago, that same government had announced plans to close the Dar-es-Salam landfill due to dangerous conditions there.</summary></entry><entry><title>DR Congo, AFC/M23 group agree on roadmap for peace negotiations after Swiss talks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:719b66e68bd88641d08ba472c2fd994cdbc28d135da9678b1a90ee7f54b4c589</id><updated>2026-08-30T15:57:07Z</updated><published>2026-08-23T12:15:29Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/africa/20260823-dr-congo-afc-m23-group-agree-on-roadmap-for-peace-negotiations-after-swiss-talks--7ff07183ac2b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20260823-dr-congo-afc-m23-group-agree-on-roadmap-for-peace-negotiations-after-swiss-talks" /><summary type="html">Mediators representing the Rwanda-backed AFC/M23 armed group and the Democratic Republic of Congo in a joint statement published Sunday said they have agreed on a roadmap for peace talks. The two sides said they had "agreed on the importance of a standardised method for reporting allegations of ceasefire violations".</summary><category term="Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Togo says it has 'serious' evidence against detained French filmmakers</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1c167524e481c085dc322d1a5ab432f91c13abfd26a013a7820a330a27b43f95</id><updated>2026-08-30T15:57:07Z</updated><published>2026-08-22T19:05:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/africa/20260822-togo-says-it-has-serious-evidence-against-detained-french-filmmakers--054ab5eac9ed.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20260822-togo-says-it-has-serious-evidence-against-detained-french-filmmakers" /><summary type="html">Togo’s government said Saturday it had “serious and corroborative evidence” against two French documentary filmmakers arrested last month alongside their Togolese fixer. The three men deny charges of making “false declarations”.</summary><category term="Africa" /></entry><entry><title>DR Congo receives Ebola vaccines in face of 'exponential' outbreak</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:650ee87ef09323e317ed76dc8b1186be973b6a3cc2c6664b98b107644abc5daa</id><updated>2026-08-30T15:57:07Z</updated><published>2026-08-22T12:47:14Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/dr-congo-receives-ebola-vaccines-in-face-of-exponential-outbreak--63c25ab7f2a0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/dr-congo-receives-ebola-vaccines-in-face-of-exponential-outbreak" /><summary type="html">The Democratic Republic of Congo has received more than 16,000 doses of an Ebola vaccine, as authorities step up efforts against the ongoing outbreak. More than 2,500 people have already died and health officials from the WHO are warning this epidemic could surpass the deadliest on record – that occurred between 2014 and 2016 and caused over 11,000 deaths across West Africa. Dr Muhammad Munir, Professor of virology at Lancaster University in the UK, helps us understand the situation on the ground.</summary></entry><entry><title>Antwerp's 'human zoo': Belgium confronts shame of colonial past</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a6aca2bbb13ea3790ac69ee122f508e3b4732c0ddc141ffa81d27c42bebb7a4a</id><updated>2026-08-30T15:57:07Z</updated><published>2026-08-22T11:05:57Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260822-antwerp-s-human-zoo-belgium-confronts-shame-of-colonial-past-1--41e55ec1ca8e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260822-antwerp-s-human-zoo-belgium-confronts-shame-of-colonial-past-1" /><summary type="html">In 1894, when the Belgian city of Antwerp was hosting a World's Fair, more than a hundred Congolese people were forcibly brought to the city to be exhibited in the Congo Pavilion. In this "human zoo", seven Congolese men ultimately died of disease. Today, this shocking episode still haunts Belgium as one of its colonial history's darkest chapters. This year, a monument to the victims was unveiled. Report by Alix le Bourbon and Dave Keating.</summary></entry><entry><title>Ethiopia uncorks a wine boom, Bordeaux vines driving exports and local demand</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2b62d5c263667d7a96788530e2cde8cc4977930f9f7591079299bdc2981e0e75</id><updated>2026-08-30T15:57:07Z</updated><published>2026-08-22T10:14:02Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/ethiopia-uncorks-a-wine-boom-bordeaux-vines-driving-exports-and-local-demand--7bd7d04f11ee.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/ethiopia-uncorks-a-wine-boom-bordeaux-vines-driving-exports-and-local-demand" /><summary type="html">A partnership between French experts and Ethiopian winemakers is putting East Africa on the viticultural map. Using seeds imported from Bordeaux, and after years of refining, exports are now on the rise. Domestically, Ethiopians are also consuming more and more of their local product. Our correspondent Tom Canetti went to meet a French-Ethiopian winery in central Ethiopia.</summary></entry><entry><title>Dozens missing after gold mine collapse in Central African Republic</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:af57f2551ccef2fa57519d8632f56dc25807478aa7bf1253553434c8d83bfc48</id><updated>2026-08-30T15:57:07Z</updated><published>2026-08-22T10:06:49Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/dozens-missing-after-gold-mine-collapse-in-central-african-republic--b66672f4bba9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/dozens-missing-after-gold-mine-collapse-in-central-african-republic" /><summary type="html">In the Central African Republic, the search for victims continues following Tuesday’s gold mine collapse. The government says the incident has claimed at least 49 lives but local sources estimate the death toll to be much higher. Cameroonian and Chadian nationals are also among the victims. Several witnesses spoke to our correspondent Marcel Amoko.</summary></entry><entry><title>Ebola epidemic in DR Congo is spreading 18 times faster than deadliest outbreak on record</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a0d1608be9208de073b7e69dc939cf9a947ba928e975af3f368efae390468364</id><updated>2026-08-30T15:57:07Z</updated><published>2026-08-22T10:06:08Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/ebola-epidemic-in-dr-congo-is-spreading-18-times-faster-than-deadliest-outbreak-on-record--c34f15ba8b5a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/ebola-epidemic-in-dr-congo-is-spreading-18-times-faster-than-deadliest-outbreak-on-record" /><summary type="html">More than 2,500 people have already died in the Ebola epidemic currently gripping the Democratic Republic of Congo. The UN coordinator for the outbreak has warned that the virus is spreading exponentially – adding that an existing pool of funds is set to run out within weeks. Details by Catherine Viette.</summary></entry><entry><title>Search continues after deadly mine collapse on Cameroon-Central African Republic border</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c5e0eb6668a5e9af494445f856943e80b13c7ea2a39043048501e07be91e20e7</id><updated>2026-08-30T15:57:07Z</updated><published>2026-08-21T20:46:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/eye-on-africa/20260821-search-continues-after-deadly-mine-collapse-on-cameroon-central-african-republic-border--f6a9f72ad9e6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/eye-on-africa/20260821-search-continues-after-deadly-mine-collapse-on-cameroon-central-african-republic-border" /><summary type="html">In tonight's edition: A deadly landslide at a gold mine in the Central African Republic leaves dozens dead, with victims from Cameroon and Chad. Meanwhile, Ethiopia is turning to Bordeaux expertise and grapevines in a bid to become East Africa's next wine destination. Finally, Belgium continues to confront its colonial past, more than a century after Congolese people were put on display at the 1894 Antwerp World's Fair.</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Ebola outbreak in DR Congo growing 'exponentially' as death toll passes 2,500</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:aa46e3d3029677202631c6526592d00b2f953ca47738f063a690d1e526406982</id><updated>2026-08-30T15:57:07Z</updated><published>2026-08-21T12:55:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/africa/20260821-ebola-outbreak-in-dr-congo-growing-exponentially-as-death-toll-passes-2-500--d70166b32556.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20260821-ebola-outbreak-in-dr-congo-growing-exponentially-as-death-toll-passes-2-500" /><summary type="html">More than half of the 2,500-plus deaths from DR Congo's Ebola outbreak have occurred within the past 20 days alone, as the virus spreads faster than any recorded outbreak, according to the UN's senior Ebola coordinator. Julien Harneis is urging a rapid scale-up of resources to prevent the epidemic from crossing into neighbouring countries.</summary><category term="Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Major Nigerian coke bust leads to arrests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:92e5c266e4127313f11c66efea9e40419efca58c5c304eca4cce964eff91a5f3</id><updated>2026-08-30T15:57:07Z</updated><published>2026-08-20T21:17:10Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/eye-on-africa/20260820-major-nigerian-coke-bust-leads-to-arrest--2c6defedb022.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/eye-on-africa/20260820-major-nigerian-coke-bust-leads-to-arrest" /><summary type="html">Nigeria's drug enforcement agency has broken up an international cocaine trafficking ring that used the continent's most populous country as a transit point for internationally bound shipments of life-devastating narcotics. Also, opponents of Tunisian President Kaïs Saïed rally in the latest in a series of pro-democracy demonstrations sparked by growing political and economic discontent. Plus we turn to Senegal for a look at the city of Saint-Louis, which sees traces of its role in the transatlantic slave trade slowly disappearing as buildings linked to the grim era are lost to neglect and urban changes.</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Cameroon's 93-year-old President Paul Biya returns after months-long stay abroad</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c9b6c2decc525231c622070c3f51265372bf6dadcb8d9d8e5711e8ed2661af18</id><updated>2026-08-30T15:57:07Z</updated><published>2026-08-20T20:19:47Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/africa/20260820-cameroon-93-year-old-president-paul-biya-returns-after-months-long-absence--724dabc4e7b3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20260820-cameroon-93-year-old-president-paul-biya-returns-after-months-long-absence" /><summary type="html">Cameroonian President Paul Biya returned to the country on Thursday after a 73-day absence, with local media reporting the 93-year-old had been in Geneva with his family and close aides. The country's opposition criticised Biya's long absence, saying he had left the country on "autopilot".</summary><category term="Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Gold mine collapse in Central African Republic leaves at least 100 dead</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d24db4861fa9b5b98cfbb12aa5f2fdb6e7b1f6b83493a4e7ed202c850ca567b6</id><updated>2026-08-30T15:57:07Z</updated><published>2026-08-20T14:22:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260820-gold-mine-collapse-in-central-african-republic-leaves-at-least-100-dead--6148ae1b27e9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260820-gold-mine-collapse-in-central-african-republic-leaves-at-least-100-dead" /><summary type="html">**This video contains sensitive content** The death toll from August 18's gold mine collapse in Zamboye, Central African Republic has surpassed 100. Several survivors were also critically injured. An investigation has been opened to determine the cause of the collapse, identify the victims and those responsible for operating the site, and establish any potential criminal liability.</summary></entry><entry><title>Angélique Kidjo makes Hollywood history as first Black African on Walk of Fame</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bf0b9566ba68fbba56d637b4191723c159ef32ab8bca605523b1a9a94e15f98c</id><updated>2026-08-30T15:57:07Z</updated><published>2026-08-19T21:36:37Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/eye-on-africa/20260819-ang_lique-kidjo-makes-hollywood-history-as-first-black-african-on-walk-of-fame--f5cb954abc5a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/eye-on-africa/20260819-ang%C3%A9lique-kidjo-makes-hollywood-history-as-first-black-african-on-walk-of-fame" /><summary type="html">Beninese music icon Angélique Kidjo celebrates her global legacy with a star on the Hollywood Walk of Fame, the first dedicated to a Black African. Also, in Nigeria, the town of Ogijo has more lead-recycling factories than anywhere else in Africa, supplying the American auto industry at a heavy cost to nearby communities. Finally, the Basilica of Our Lady of Peace in Ivory Coast is the world's largest church. Beneath its immense dome, temperatures can fall to just 22°C; a breath of fresh air for worshippers.</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Central African Republic gold mine collapse kills more than 100</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:73020f7dd86c93e717e0c6d622885d7bd889a189a79accec8af0d1df0b5ea483</id><updated>2026-08-30T15:57:07Z</updated><published>2026-08-19T19:36:10Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/africa/20260819-more-than-100-killed-central-african-republic-gold-mine-collapse--16e409b91976.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20260819-more-than-100-killed-central-african-republic-gold-mine-collapse" /><summary type="html">A gold mine collapse in the Central African Republican village of Zamboye near the Cameroon border on Tuesday killed more than 100 people, an official at a local mining association said. A member of the local youth council said the death toll would likely rise as more people were pulled from the rubble.</summary><category term="Africa" /></entry></feed>
